<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-11-07T20:20:31Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Armenia's selective prosecution: A threat to EU relations?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e718256ac1910487152a2d1891722253716af4bb94c8082a36f5abd361b31188</id><updated>2026-11-07T20:20:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T18:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/armenia-s-selective-prosecution-a-threat-to-eu-relations/a-79878159--345ae9a3ae32.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/armenia-s-selective-prosecution-a-threat-to-eu-relations/a-79878159?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While Brussels has refrained from harsh criticism, Armenian civil society has warned of selective justice against opposition figures. Could the EU's pragmatic stance risk repeating past mistakes?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa's ANC facing worst-ever performance in local elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6f0641d2d4c3a71910b052e4959207e70fec154f381f7c53cc08be1c0a9d27d</id><updated>2026-11-07T20:20:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T18:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-africa-s-anc-facing-worst-ever-performance-in-local-elections/a-79887482--0f01de17e4d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-africa-s-anc-facing-worst-ever-performance-in-local-elections/a-79887482?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Near-final results show South Africa's once dominant ANC will see its lowest-ever vote percentage. The party is taking the blame for shoddy municipal services, including water and electricity shortages.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Journalism and AI: Who owns the news?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:650d97ce8864e6c1abf4df39a54d2b35dcb9bd2763eac35eaf7ac94b09808067</id><updated>2026-11-07T20:20:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T15:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/journalism-and-ai-who-owns-the-news/a-79884854--eca12d826319.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/journalism-and-ai-who-owns-the-news/a-79884854?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Publishers say AI chatbots are using their reporting to answer readers' questions while sending back less traffic and less money. Should the companies that build these tools pay for the journalism they rely on?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Son of Iran's shah receives 'Freedom Prize' in Frankfurt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8c898f93118baf28124cc65b350aa84c2d6eb7dc9f5ce8eb394705661131531</id><updated>2026-11-07T20:19:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T14:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/son-of-iran-s-shah-receives-freedom-prize-in-frankfurt/a-79885661--aa99dccac573.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/son-of-iran-s-shah-receives-freedom-prize-in-frankfurt/a-79885661?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">18,000 people gathered in Frankfurt to show support for Reza Pahlavi, the son of the Iranian monarch ousted in 1979. Factions in the opposition have accused him of not distancing himself from his father's rule.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>After victory in the midterms, what next for US Democrats?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d21a200ae8f7436078995eac0ea3afbe1ad135221497618a6dbe066f943c2452</id><updated>2026-11-07T20:19:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T14:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-victory-in-the-midterms-what-next-for-us-democrats/a-79884957--f8ad14f3dbbf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-victory-in-the-midterms-what-next-for-us-democrats/a-79884957?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's Republican party has lost its majority in both chambers of the US Congress. But the president still has a lot of power — and the Democrats have yet to agree on how best to use theirs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Russia hits Kyiv with airstrikes ahead of trilateral talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2012b30d1224490c803a8c5d601ea8a14be50d0e3d009b88a6af8554921ef9b</id><updated>2026-11-07T20:19:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T09:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-hits-kyiv-with-airstrikes-ahead-of-trilateral-talks/a-79883851--55817e315a75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-hits-kyiv-with-airstrikes-ahead-of-trilateral-talks/a-79883851?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The strikes hit a major bridge and energy facilities in the Kyiv region. President Volodymyr Zelenskyy accused Moscow of trying to "push" Ukraine "into a blackout" ahead of talks in Abu Dhabi.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Amid protests, France's rising debt costs threaten stability</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8da0816cbcfa0f3402033a3f44819465b9c262bd59aa265319b2bfc5b0c0b527</id><updated>2026-11-07T20:19:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/amid-protests-france-s-rising-debt-costs-threaten-stability/a-79865654--50648477f294.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/amid-protests-france-s-rising-debt-costs-threaten-stability/a-79865654?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France plans to spend an extra €4 billion on education amid nationwide protests. But with public debt mounting and interest costs climbing, how much fiscal room does the government have?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>US: Giant pandas from China make public debut at Atlanta zoo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa71c84bc2828043380941ab8c44f268cd86cf4700854422e0c216a491a22944</id><updated>2026-11-07T20:19:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T07:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-giant-pandas-from-china-make-public-debut-at-atlanta-zoo/a-79883388--b468c87ae7ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-giant-pandas-from-china-make-public-debut-at-atlanta-zoo/a-79883388?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ping Ping and Fu Shuang are the first giant pandas to be housed in Zoo Atlanta after a gap of two years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US asks China to uphold Busan trade deal commitments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c3fc910f4be670afa4f07d6d03948d45e03963d230599fb78deb72212aa912c</id><updated>2026-11-07T20:19:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T04:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-asks-china-to-uphold-busan-trade-deal-commitments/a-79882939--7107d3b9b548.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-asks-china-to-uphold-busan-trade-deal-commitments/a-79882939?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US urged Beijing to meet commitments from a 2025 accord — particularly on agricultural purchases and rare earths supply. China, meanwhile, expressed concern over the US' "economic, trade restrictive" measures.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ueno Bank scandal plunges Paraguay into political crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed3ef54d71578b42a340a3a407172fb6a9e75e9d20dfbf1854687d8ff3debf3f</id><updated>2026-11-07T20:19:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T20:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ueno-bank-scandal-plunges-paraguay-into-political-crisis/a-79881388--35a7e5f2572b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ueno-bank-scandal-plunges-paraguay-into-political-crisis/a-79881388?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Suspected financial fraud, public money at risk and millions of customers affected: Paraguay is in serious crisis following the sudden collapse of Ueno Bank. President Santiago Pena is facing impeachment.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Critics say Democrats should look into Trump's Middle East deals in future corruption investigations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8d7b7b61dbf6dfbc17db4c0ede650c47a5d6492895b9ea7aecd71f486a586eb</id><updated>2026-11-07T20:19:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T19:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/critics-say-democrats-should-look-into-trump-s-middle-east-deals-in-future-corruption-investigations/a-79877104--54038fc6b2c6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/critics-say-democrats-should-look-into-trump-s-middle-east-deals-in-future-corruption-investigations/a-79877104?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After their victory in the US midterm elections, the Democrats have promised to investigate corruption in the Trump administration. Critics say the president's Middle East deals is an area they should focus on.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Czech arms makers set sights on space defense in bid to sustain Ukraine-driven arms boom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d7f9a556995fd52a4f0a7d724a6f93428f55db0b728035917edb2119666c34a</id><updated>2026-11-07T20:19:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T14:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/czech-arms-makers-set-sights-on-space-defense-in-bid-to-sustain-ukraine-driven-arms-boom/a-79876035--897a0df46a70.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/czech-arms-makers-set-sights-on-space-defense-in-bid-to-sustain-ukraine-driven-arms-boom/a-79876035?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Czech arms makers have thrived on demand linked to the war in Ukraine. To sustain their growth, they need to look beyond ammunition and toward new technologies — and even space.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Zambia's opposition criticizes government restructuring and layoffs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c043148d89a8381077b648bae2b1114e096df533cf4d00b37ea174737bdc7172</id><updated>2026-11-07T20:19:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/zambia-s-opposition-criticizes-government-restructuring-and-layoffs/a-79875892--f6feaaea394e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/zambia-s-opposition-criticizes-government-restructuring-and-layoffs/a-79875892?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Government-backed dismissals and restructuring are fueling debate in Zambia. Opposition politicians are questioning the transparency of the plans; officials say the changes are necessary.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
